# Cloud-role TLS reverse proxy (ticket B1 design 9) -- HTTP Basic Auth
# over plain HTTP would leak the password in transit, in tension with
# docs/pilot/data-agreement-outline.md's "encryption in transit"
# commitment. Caddy gets automatic Let's Encrypt TLS from ~5 lines of
# config -- still "cheap single VM," not IaC-scale ceremony.
#
# Vessel-role instances do NOT need this (deploy/README.md) -- they bind
# to the ship LAN/localhost only, never the public internet, matching
# TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md §8's "no internet exposure of the edge
# device" principle.
#
# Replace with your real domain, then: caddy run --config Caddyfile

your-cloud-instance.example.com {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
